Photorealistic vintage 1980s Japanese Hi-Fi audio user-interface asset: one single long horizontal progress bar channel, viewed perfectly straight-on, centered, spanning 90 percent of the image width and about one quarter of its height, isolated on a pure flat black background. Shape: long horizontal rectangular cassette tape well plate with clean precision corners. Frame: brushed champagne-silver aluminum bezel with fine bevels and stainless screws at left and right ends. Inside: a recessed channel of dark smoked grey acrylic. Running the full length of the channel, a musical staff of exactly five thin, perfectly straight, evenly spaced, parallel horizontal lines made of fine glowing fluorescent teal VFD display lines. At the far left of the staff, one stylized treble clef illuminated in glowing coral-red VFD light. Nothing else on the staff: no notes, no bar lines, no numbers, no text. Clean product photography, crisp focus. One object only, no watermark.
